  (text "LAMPS ARE ACTIVE LOW.\nAnode to +5V through Rn, cathode to GPBn.\nDriving GPBn LOW lights the lamp; the pins idle HIGH.\nWiring a lamp the other way round inverts the whole panel." (at 12.0 200.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4bda5412-d6a7-4224-811d-a5c095912ef4"))
  (text "R1-R7 set lamp current from the 5V rail:\n  220R -> 9mA (white/blue, Vf 3.0V), 13mA (green/yellow), 14mA (red)\n  470R -> about half that, if they are too bright for a bedroom\nWorst case 7 x 14mA = 95mA, inside the MCP23017's 150mA package limit\nand far inside its 25mA per-pin limit." (at 12.0 218.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "fc8486a4-82c6-45d2-bbb4-e30994284e6e"))
  (text "DO NOT FIT I2C PULL-UPS. The Pi already has 1.8k on SDA and SCL.\nA0/A1/A2 to GND selects address 0x20. RESET must be tied high -\nleft floating it glitches and looks like phantom button presses.\nGPA7/GPB7 and INTA/INTB are spare; the driver polls at 50Hz." (at 12.0 242.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d501da5a-56c1-4d3a-aa3c-c9cdce860ed1"))
  (text "Unused header pins are left open on purpose: this board stacks under\nthe ReSpeaker HAT, which uses I2S (18-21), I2C (2-3) and SPI (7-11)." (at 12.0 262.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a53ebdc9-4b10-497e-a872-1a6b5834dca7"))
  (sheet_instances
    (path "/" (page "1")))
